   284	### 4.1 Proposition 4, printed without proof — REPAIRED
   285	
   286	At a target nodal vertex of valence \(r\ge3\), let \(k_i\) be the number of
   287	points of \(\widetilde a\) above its \(i\)-th incident direction.  Riemann--
   288	Hurwitz gives
   289	
   290	\[
   291	\sum_i k_i=(r-2)m+2.                                     \tag{4.8}
   292	\]
   293	
   294	If source and target valences agree, the left side is \(r\), so
   295	\((r-2)(m-1)=0\), hence \(m=1\).  Conversely \(m=1\) gives one unramified
   296	longitudinal contact in every direction, equality of valences, and incident
   297	chain degree \(n=\operatorname{Deg}\widetilde a\).  Finally, if every
   298	incident chain has degree \(mn\), every local index is \(m\), so every fiber
   299	has one point and (4.8) again gives \(m=1\).  This proves the printed
   300	equivalence of Proposition 4(a)--(c).
