   586	`(1)`-`(2)` and `(3)` are **different instruments on different objects**: the
   587	first two constrain the ACS-1 monodromy of a (B3) profile; the third
   588	constrains an explicit pullback normal form at one cell of the horn's
   589	`A`-degree-2 census. They do not compose into a kill, and I do not claim one.
