   609	1. `OPEN[DEG-AF-VS-N]` (MI §9). A bound `deg bar A_F <= f(N)` turns the
   610	   `delta`-budget `delta(p,q) + sum_i t_i + delta_infty = (n-1)(n-2)/2` into a
   611	   bound on `k` and on the Puiseux pair, and Prop 3.2 then leaves a finite
   612	   list at `N = 4`. This is the single highest-value successor for (B3).
   613	2. A `(B3)` analogue of CUSP-KILL for `j = 1`. THEOREM B3-N4 hands it the exact
   614	   object to work on: an irreducible affine `E` of genus `k_odd-1` with one
   615	   quasi-homogeneous cusp and `3+4k-2k_odd` places at infinity, index 4 and
   616	   non-normal in `G`. Case (A)'s route through Lin-Zaidenberg is unavailable;
   617	   a route through the ends is not.
   618	3. `(O0, O1)` on the A2 `E1`-wall. THEOREM HORN-A2 reduces
   619	   `OBSTRUCTION[A-DEGREE-TWO]` to one wall with rigid leaders; two unconsumed
   620	   equations remain, and the `y : w = 3 : 4` pin is exactly the kind of datum
   621	   a subleading pass can contradict.
