+| 12 | Polynomial compactification; source root maps to infinity; `K~=F^*K+B`, with boundary-supported Jacobian divisor | root lies in `L~_infty`; coefficient at `g~` is `n(g~)-1` | Root containment is degree-free. The replay's numerical coefficient `1` assumes `n(g~)=2`; at `mu=3` it is `2`. |
+| 13 | Maximal Deg-2 block `Delta`; first nodal vertex on a specified path; transfer value `det(v_1 g)=2`; root placement; strict Russian “linear” meaning ambient valence at most two | the indicated intersection/path is linear | **Conditional Deg-2/`n(g)=2` schema, not a promoted all-N lemma.** In the `d>1` branch unity comes from root-unit Lemma 3, not positivity Lemma 4. |
+| 14 | Lemma 13 plus root assumed in `Delta`; graph value/lower bound `det L~_infty>=-2`; canonical decomposition | root is outside `Delta` | **Not unconditional or all-N.** It inherits Lemma 13 and the fixed-graph determinant hypothesis. |
+| 15 | Exact Figs. 20/21; Proposition-2 calculation `det L~_infty=-1`; Lemmas 13–14; `B>=1`, omitted branch product `C>=3`, `alpha>=1` | (7.10), `-1<=-4`, contradiction | **Not degree-free as a graph kill.** The floors are degree-free; `det=-1`, `C>=3`, and the closed graph are specific. |
+
