   101	## 2. Raw census: exact enumeration
   102	
   103	### 2.1 Definition
   104	
   105	For a fork of longitudinal degree `m>=2` and transverse degree `n>=1`, let
   106	`lambda_L,lambda_R,lambda_D` be the three partitions of `m` recording the
   107	longitudinal contact indices. If `ell(lambda)` denotes length, fork
   108	Riemann–Hurwitz is
   109	
   110	```text
   111	ell(lambda_L)+ell(lambda_R)+ell(lambda_D)=m+2.
   112	```
   113	
   114	The printed degrees on the incident constant tubes are `n` times the parts.
   115	Thus, with `P(m,r)` the number of partitions of `m` into exactly `r` parts,
   116	
   117	```text
   118	f_m(z)   = sum_{r>=1} P(m,r) z^r,
   119	Rows(m)  = [z^(m+2)] f_m(z)^3,
   120	Census(N)= sum_{m=2}^N floor(N/m) Rows(m).
   121	```
   122	
   123	The triples are ordered by the labelled directions `L|R|D`; only the entries
   124	inside one partition are unordered. This is precisely DR's encoding
   125	(`DR:328–360`) and the reviewed closed form (`BR:185–196`).
   126	
