   176	## 3. The `(B3)` charged profiles and their fibres
   177	
   178	### 3.1 Exact finite generator
   179	
   180	Put `W=N-a`. At `N=5,6`, `2 sum s_l<=W` with every `mu_l>=2` forces one
   181	dicritical with `s=1`; it is `(s,mu)=(1,W)`. Hence `R=sum(s_l-1)=0`.
   182	For a charged singular point write
   183	
   184	```text
   185	P=(r,K,a_p),                  a_p=N-r W-K.
   186	C_K=(1,K,a-K),                a cusp,
   187	M_{r,K}=(r,K,N-r W-K),        a charged multibranch point.
   188	```
   189	
   190	The exact rules are `K>=1`, `a_p>=0`, `sum K=a-1`, and at least one cusp.
   191	The `(B3)` cell also contains a multibranch point. Following the charged
   192	producer/review convention, the finite list records only the `K>0` points and
   193	uses one neutral double point
   194	
   195	```text
   196	U_2=(2,0,N-2W)
   197	```
   198	
   199	as the displayed multibranch representative when needed. Further `K=0`
   200	multibranch points are not bounded by `(K)` and are not new charged cells. Thus
   201	`3` and `9` are finite **charged-skeleton** counts, not counts of all singular
   202	configurations. This distinction is forced by `BI:696–699`.
   203	
   204	The rules come from BI-1/7.B' (`MI:82–88`), the fibre law `(L)` and total law
   205	`(K)` (`MI:222–272`), localization Lemmas 4.2–4.3 (`MI:275–294`), and THEOREM
   206	PROFILE (`MI:413–438`). The reviewed lists and caps are `BR:235–265`.
   207	
   208	Because `s=1`, each branch over `p` has one dicritical point with local excess
   209	`k_b`, and its escaping fibre part is `mu+k_b`. Therefore the full affine fibre
   210	partition at `p` is
   211	
   212	```text
   213	1^(a_p)  +  (mu+k_1,...,mu+k_r),       sum k_b=K.
   214	```
   215	
   216	This is the pointwise fibre law, not a boundary `v_0` profile.
