+
+The requested either/or outcome is the second branch, with an important
+qualification: the frozen data determine exact **seed families**, not exact
+completed global graphs.
+
+| degree/profile | raw rows | unresolved first-fork seeds | lemma firing now | boundary datum still needed |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| N=5, each of 3 cells | 86 | **35** | none | `DO-PORT-ATTACH-N5`, then fixed-graph determinant audit |
+| N=6, cells 6.1–6.2 | 287 | **85** | none | `DO-PORT-ATTACH-N6`, `DO-MU3-CANONICAL-BLOCK`, then audit |
+| N=6, cells 6.3–6.9 | 287 | **126** | none | `DO-PORT-ATTACH-N6`, then audit |
+| N=4 control | 35 | 13 before N=4 determinant pruning; 4 legal first-fork rows | Lemma 10 on 24/25; Lemma 11 on 22/23; Lemmas 12–15 on 20/21 | none for the `(mu,corr)=(2,1)` kill |
+
+Accordingly:
+
+```text
+FIRST EMPTY WINDOW IN N FOR (B3):  NOT ESTABLISHED.
+N=5: no Lemma-10–15 analogue has a graph on which it legally fires.
+N=6: same; the a=3 branch additionally changes the canonical coefficient.
