   400	### 4.4 Why no further row count is licensed
   401	
   402	DR explicitly warns that a partition part records a **contact, not a vertex**:
   403	it may end, continue to a fork, or reach the dicritical, and these alternatives
   404	are resolved only after determinant transfer, coprimality, and `sum Deg=N`
   405	(`DR:328–340`). A concrete control is the row `11|2|2`: repeated left
   406	determinants kill it only if both contacts end; DR instead forces at least one
   407	to continue and holds the row for the degree-three census (`DR:366–381`).
   408	Therefore a screen that kills every repeated `1` before assigning endpoint
   409	classes is false.
   410	
   411	At `N=4`, the subsequent pruning repeatedly uses consequences of the value
   412	four: a forced endpoint has total degree `4`, a parallel packet makes a Lemma-7
   413	lower bound exceed `4`, or Corollary 4 removes a Deg-2 fork
   414	(`DR:364–482`). At `N=5,6` those conclusions change. In particular, BR forbids
   415	a general-`N` Corollary 4 (`BR:269–280`). The repaired attachment says the
   416	dicritical is incident to Lemma 6's constant block; it does not turn Corollary
   417	4 into an all-degree fork theorem (`BR:60–86`).
