+`(4,2)`, while `(1,1)` gives `(3,3)`. Neither BI-4 nor B3-CAGE selects one,
+so the displayed two-element set is exact.
+
+The three-cusp cap `-1` says `p_a(E)<=-1`, hence `j>=2`; it does not say the
+cell is empty (`BR:149–161`). More neutral nodes increase the displayed cap,
+so the table must not be read as an equality for an arbitrary number of
+neutral points.
