+### 5.3 What survives at N=5 and N=6
+
+No lemma in the preceding table fires on an `N=5` or `N=6` seed merely from
+its row. There is no identified analogue graph on which to substitute the
+numeric calculation. The exact surviving boundary families are therefore
+finite but unresolved extension families:
+
+```text
+G_5(P)      = extensions of the 35 first-fork seeds, depth <=3,
+              for each P in {5.1,5.2,5.3};
+G_6,3(P)    = extensions of the 85 first-fork seeds, depth <=3,
+              for P in {6.1,6.2};
+G_6,4(P)    = extensions of the 126 first-fork seeds, depth <=4,
+              for P in {6.3,...,6.9}.
+```
+
+“Extension” here means assigning each contact an endpoint class, gluing equal
+tube degrees without a cycle, adding the companion components required by
+`sum Deg=N` at every target vertex, locating the source root, and then imposing
+Lemma-5 transfer, determinant coprimality, repaired Lemma 7, and the edge and
+canonical formulas. This definition states the remaining task; it does not
+pretend that the extensions have been enumerated.
+
+The missing input is finite and can be typed precisely. Across the raw
+catalogs there are `549` contact-port occurrences at `N=5` and `2127` at
+`N=6`. Grouping by printed tube degree gives:
+
+```text
+N=5: q=1..5 port counts   228,156,81,54,30;
+N=6: q=1..6 port counts   810,612,336,195,99,75.
+```
+
+There are therefore at most `43,074` and `597,432` unordered distinct
+equal-degree port pairs to classify before the depth cap. This is comfortably
+desk-scale once the mathematical endpoint/transition predicate is stated.
+
+```text
+OPEN[DO-PORT-ATTACH-N5]
+bounded quantity: terminal/continuing compatibility on 549 typed ports,
+                  with at most 43,074 equal-degree port pairs and depth 3.
+
+OPEN[DO-PORT-ATTACH-N6]
+bounded quantity: terminal/continuing compatibility on 2,127 typed ports,
+                  with at most 597,432 equal-degree port pairs and depth 3 or 4.
+
+OPEN[DO-DET-CANONICAL-N5-N6]
+bounded quantity: one exact integer determinant/canonical audit per graph
+                  emitted by the two finite transition tables.  A single
+                  spine has at most a(N+2) incident slots (21 at N=5,
+                  24 or 32 at N=6); the whole branching-tree bound is below.
+
+OPEN[DO-MU3-CANONICAL-BLOCK]
+bounded quantity: one rederivation of Lemmas 13–14 with incident Deg 3 and
+                  canonical coefficient mu-1=2, for profiles 6.1–6.2.
+```
+
+The domains of determinant variables need not be guessed or artificially
+capped: the bounded object is the yes/no exact audit of each fixed emitted
+graph. BI-8 caps forks per root-to-leaf spine, not total forks in a branching
+tree. Since a fork has at most `N+2` contacts, the number of fork vertices in a
+compressed rooted tree is bounded by
+
+```text
+Kmax(N,a)=1+(N+1)+...+(N+1)^(a-1)=((N+1)^a-1)/N:
+Kmax(5,3)=43; Kmax(6,3)=57; Kmax(6,4)=400.
+```
+
+A deliberately coarse finite bound on labelled compressed endpoint
+assignments is therefore
+
+```text
+B(N,a)=sum_{k=1}^Kmax Census(N)^k * (k(N+2)+2)^(k(N+2)).
+```
+
+For each of at most `k` fork rows, every port is assigned a terminal/`g`/typed
+port destination. Tree, degree, direction, and determinant tests only reduce
+this overcount. The corresponding whole-tree incident-slot bounds are `301`,
+`456`, and `3,200`. Until `DO-PORT-ATTACH` is supplied, there is no graph list
+on which to run those audits.
+
+`OPEN[BI-TAIL-AT-INFINITY]` remains one yes/no for the unique dicritical in
+each cell: whether an F-constant component of `L~_infty` maps to `p`. It gates
+BI-3/BI-5 saturation only; it does not weaken BI-1, BI-5-Deg, the first-fork
+catalog, or BI-8 (`BR:121–141,275–280`). BI-ATTACH itself is repaired and is
+not reopened.
+
