+### 5.3 What survives at N=5 and N=6
+
+No lemma in the preceding table fires on an `N=5` or `N=6` seed merely from
+its row. There is no identified analogue graph on which to substitute the
+numeric calculation. Consuming the review's bounded-successor conclusion at
+its confirmed scope (`BR:269–274`), the candidate families are finite but
+their members have not been derived:
+
+```text
+G_5(P)      = bounded extensions of 67 any-direction row types
+              (35 in the conditional R subcatalog), P in {5.1,5.2,5.3};
+G_6,3(P)    = bounded extensions of 181 types (conditional R: 85),
+              P in {6.1,6.2};
+G_6,4(P)    = bounded extensions of 238 types (conditional R: 126),
+              P in {6.3,...,6.9}.
+```
+
+“Extension” here means assigning each contact an endpoint class, gluing equal
+tube degrees without a cycle, adding the companion components required by
+`sum Deg=N` at every target vertex, locating the source root, and then imposing
+Lemma-5 transfer, determinant coprimality, repaired Lemma 7, and the edge and
+canonical formulas. This definition states the remaining task; it does not
+pretend that the extensions have been enumerated. BI-8 gives per-spine fork
+caps `3`, `3`, and `4` in the three windows; those are not whole-tree depths.
+
+The missing derivation can be typed precisely. Across the raw catalogs there
+are `549` contact-port occurrences at `N=5` and `2127` at `N=6`. Grouping by
+printed tube degree gives:
+
+```text
+N=5: q=1..5 port counts   228,156,81,54,30;
+N=6: q=1..6 port counts   810,612,336,195,99,75.
+```
+
+Including diagonal reuse (needed already by N=4 Fig. 25), the equal-degree
+projection contains `sum_q c_q^2 = 86,697` and `1,196,991` ordered pairs.
+These are reproducible diagnostics only. Endpoint compatibility also depends
+on downstream branch state and root placement, so they are not bounds on
+transition cases or global graphs.
+
+```text
+OPEN[DO-ENDPOINT-N5]
+bounded quantity: one finite endpoint/continuation/root-state specification
+                  over 86 row types and 549 labelled port occurrences; its
+                  equal-degree projection has 86,697 ordered pairs.
+
+OPEN[DO-ENDPOINT-N6]
+bounded quantity: one finite endpoint/continuation/root-state specification
+                  over 287 row types and 2,127 labelled port occurrences; its
+                  equal-degree projection has 1,196,991 ordered pairs.
+
+OPEN[DO-GLOBAL-FORK-BOUND]
+bounded quantity: one proof that all relevant forks are covered by BI-8's
+                  controlled spines, or three explicit total-fork bounds for
+                  (N,a)=(5,3),(6,3),(6,4).  BI-8 alone is per-spine.
+
+OPEN[DO-DET-CANONICAL-N5-N6]
+bounded quantity: one exact integer determinant/canonical audit per graph
+                  emitted by the review-certified finite assembly after the
+                  endpoint and total-fork derivations are supplied.
+
+OPEN[DO-MU3-CANONICAL-BLOCK]
+bounded quantity: one rederivation of Lemmas 13–14 with incident Deg 3 and
+                  canonical coefficient mu-1=2, for profiles 6.1–6.2.
+```
+
+The determinant variables themselves are not capped by analogy. The bounded
+object is a binary exact audit for each fixed graph in the finite list promised
+by the review. The five frozen inputs provide no valid numerical cardinality
+bound for that whole-graph list: multiplying the per-spine BI-8 cap by a local
+port count would silently turn “on a spine” into “in the tree.”
+
+`OPEN[BI-TAIL-AT-INFINITY]` remains one yes/no for the sole dicritical in each
+of the 12 displayed N=5/6 charged cells: whether an F-constant component of
+`L~_infty` maps to `p`. It gates BI-3/BI-5 saturation only; it does not weaken
+BI-1, BI-5-Deg, the incidence catalogs, or BI-8 (`BR:121–141,275–280`).
+BI-ATTACH itself is repaired and is not reopened.
